Package: postrank
Type: Package
Title: Posterior Ranking with Integer Grades
Version: 1.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("JoonHo", "Lee", email = "jlee296@ua.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-4019-8703"))
Description: Assigns integer grades to entities using posterior information
    for one or several criteria, a specified directional loss and a cost for
    withheld comparisons. A common grading is obtained when several criteria
    are considered. Multidomain profiles instead retain a separate grade per
    domain, using additive losses and direct joint-event protection over a
    declared finite candidate family. Exact policy arithmetic, fixed-report
    iid assessment and descriptive MCMC diagnostics are provided for profiles.
    Inputs include validated equal-weight draws, exact finite laws,
    conditional Gaussian laws, shared-state Gaussian mixtures and previously
    calculated tie-free comparison probabilities. Model estimation is conducted separately. Optional modes
    add error budgets, minimax decisions, exact grade counts and a separate
    equality-neutral loss where supported. The default solver is 'Gurobi';
    'HiGHS' is an explicit alternative. Data loading and the display of stored
    results do not require either backend. Results retain validated grades,
    numerical solver bounds, criterion profiles and input-aware diagnostics.
    Seven common-grade 'ggplot2' figures and three profile views, English reports,
    applied and methodological
    articles and three case studies are provided
    for interpretation. The method builds on the integer-grade report card of
    Kline, Rose and Walters (2024) <doi:10.1257/aer.20230700>.
